1264
01:53:41.290 --> 01:53:44.290
He has been present in the proximity of Jesus.

1265
01:53:44.290 --> 01:53:48.290
He probably helped distribute bread and fish.

1266
01:53:48.290 --> 01:53:51.290
He has seen the miracle happen before his eyes.

1267
01:53:51.290 --> 01:53:53.290
Hop, more bread.

1268
01:53:53.290 --> 01:53:58.290
He was probably there when people were raised from the dead.

1269
01:53:58.290 --> 01:54:00.290
He has been everywhere.

1270
01:54:00.290 --> 01:54:03.290
Judas has been everywhere.

1271
01:54:03.290 --> 01:54:05.290
It can't get closer than Judas.

1272
01:54:06.290 --> 01:54:09.290
Judas was there. He was in the group.

1273
01:54:10.290 --> 01:54:15.290
But Judas allowed something to grow in his heart.

1274
01:54:15.290 --> 01:54:19.290
Which ultimately led to his corruption.

1275
01:54:19.290 --> 01:54:24.290
And eventually even, as the Bible says, the entrance of Satan into his spirit.

1276
01:54:25.290 --> 01:54:29.290
When it was the conscious night that Jesus was crucified.

1277
01:54:29.290 --> 01:54:31.290
That period, sorry.

1278
01:54:31.290 --> 01:54:36.290
The conscious period of the arrest of Jesus.

1279
01:54:36.290 --> 01:54:40.290
Then the Bible says that Satan entered into Judas.

1280
01:54:40.290 --> 01:54:43.290
And this is an important thing for us Christians.

1281
01:54:43.290 --> 01:54:48.290
Can Christians or can people who are with God, can they be possessed?

1282
01:54:48.290 --> 01:54:51.290
And the answer is yes and no.

1283
01:54:51.290 --> 01:54:58.290
It is very difficult for us to see when the moment is that Satan actually comes into you.

1284
01:54:58.290 --> 01:55:04.290
First, you create a breeding ground for Satan to be able to tempt you with something.

1285
01:55:04.290 --> 01:55:07.290
First, a false thought comes.

1286
01:55:07.290 --> 01:55:11.290
First, someone has done something to you and you create a kind of bitterness.

1287
01:55:11.290 --> 01:55:14.290
And you say to yourself, I will never be able to forgive him.

1288
01:55:14.290 --> 01:55:17.290
As soon as you start saying that, a breeding ground arises.

1289
01:55:18.290 --> 01:55:21.290
Then you are not immediately possessed by Satan.

1290
01:55:21.290 --> 01:55:25.290
But you begin with a breeding ground that is not the same as God's kingdom.

1291
01:55:25.290 --> 01:55:27.290
That is where it starts.

1292
01:55:27.290 --> 01:55:30.290
What are you beginning to sow in your soul?

1293
01:55:30.290 --> 01:55:32.290
What is allowed to come in?

1294
01:55:32.290 --> 01:55:35.290
Yes, I am married to that woman, but she is this.

1295
01:55:35.290 --> 01:55:37.290
And then you start to sow in your soul.

1296
01:55:37.290 --> 01:55:43.290
And ultimately we see in the life of Judas, and the Bible does not provide broad evidence...

1297
01:55:43.290 --> 01:55:47.290
...about what actually went wrong in the life of Judas.

1298
01:55:47.290 --> 01:55:50.290
What he might have expected from Jesus.

1299
01:55:50.290 --> 01:55:54.290
In some films we see that they think Judas thought...

1300
01:55:54.290 --> 01:55:58.290
...that Jesus would be a Davidic military king.

1301
01:55:58.290 --> 01:56:02.290
And that Judas is then disappointed that Jesus is not actually that way.

1302
01:56:02.290 --> 01:56:05.290
And that he therefore goes to the chief priest to say...

1303
01:56:05.290 --> 01:56:09.290
...you know what, I will sell him, because this is not the Jesus I had hoped for.

1304
01:56:09.290 --> 01:56:12.290
That's nice, that's speculative, that's not what the Bible says.

1305
01:56:12.290 --> 01:56:18.290
The Bible does say that Judas took money from the treasury, stealing from the treasury of Jesus.

1306
01:56:18.290 --> 01:56:20.290
Completely crazy.

1307
01:56:35.290 --> 01:56:38.290
Judas stole from the treasury of Jesus.

1308
01:56:39.290 --> 01:56:45.290
While you are with him, you should take money away from Jesus.

1309
01:56:46.290 --> 01:56:49.290
What do you think? It's Jesus.

1310
01:56:49.290 --> 01:56:51.290
It's Jesus.

1311
01:56:51.290 --> 01:56:56.290
Do you need money? Then go to that river, there is a fish.

1312
01:56:56.290 --> 01:56:59.290
There is about 1500 euros in that fish.

1313
01:56:59.290 --> 01:57:01.290
It's Jesus.

1314
01:57:01.290 --> 01:57:05.290
Jesus who says, are we hungry? 15,000 people.

1315
01:57:06.290 --> 01:57:09.290
I will take care of food, says Jesus.

1316
01:57:09.290 --> 01:57:11.290
You know what? Here we go.

1317
01:57:11.290 --> 01:57:14.290
Do you know what it costs, what Jesus has done?

1318
01:57:14.290 --> 01:57:17.290
Jesus, the Son of God, everything was from him.

1319
01:57:17.290 --> 01:57:21.290
And still you have to steal from the treasury of the Lord.

1320
01:57:21.290 --> 01:57:23.290
What do you think?

1321
01:57:23.290 --> 01:57:26.290
So Judas had something rotten in his soul.

1322
01:57:26.290 --> 01:57:28.290
He was becoming rotten.

1323
01:57:28.290 --> 01:57:32.290
He was corrupt in the presence of Jesus.

1324
01:57:33.290 --> 01:57:40.290
Dear Open Church, being in the presence of Open Church says nothing about your heart condition.

1325
01:57:40.290 --> 01:57:45.290
You can always come here, but stay with Jesus with a pure heart.

1326
01:57:45.290 --> 01:57:50.290
Pray, as far as I'm concerned, just like I do, every day the Our Father with sincere words.

1327
01:57:50.290 --> 01:57:52.290
Mean what you say, what you pray.

1328
01:57:52.290 --> 01:57:55.290
And please say, Lord, keep my heart pure.

1329
01:57:55.290 --> 01:57:59.290
Keep my heart pure, for I do not want to fall away like Judas.

1330
01:57:59.290 --> 01:58:02.290
He could have been one of the greats.

1331
01:58:02.290 --> 01:58:06.290
What does it say here? Verse 17. Look again with me.

1332
01:58:06.290 --> 01:58:10.290
He was part of our group and had the same task as we did.

1333
01:58:10.290 --> 01:58:15.290
He could have been an amazing guy in God's kingdom.

1334
01:58:15.290 --> 01:58:21.290
But God does not look at your potential, which is so often said in the Christian church.

1335
01:58:21.290 --> 01:58:23.290
Oh, He has potential for you.

1336
01:58:23.290 --> 01:58:27.290
Yes, potential. Yes, of course God has a purpose for you.

1337
01:58:27.290 --> 01:58:30.290
But you must remain pure.

1338
01:58:30.290 --> 01:58:34.290
Stay with Jesus.

1339
01:58:34.290 --> 01:58:38.290
So often I look through Open Church.

1340
01:58:38.290 --> 01:58:41.290
So often I see people passing through the church.

1341
01:58:41.290 --> 01:58:43.290
People who come and people who go.

1342
01:58:43.290 --> 01:58:49.290
So often I see people that I think to myself, oh the potential I see in such a guy.

1343
01:58:49.290 --> 01:58:55.290
I have seen young men come by that I thought, wow, this could be such an amazing youth pastor.

1344
01:58:55.290 --> 01:58:59.290
This guy, with the charisma that person has.

1345
01:58:59.290 --> 01:59:03.290
And with the language and communicative skills that such a person has.

1346
01:59:03.290 --> 01:59:06.290
This could have been an amazing evangelist.

1347
01:59:06.290 --> 01:59:08.290
This could have been a youth pastor.

1348
01:59:08.290 --> 01:59:11.290
Who could have taken crowds of youth with him.

1349
01:59:11.290 --> 01:59:13.290
But it is not your potential that saves you.

1350
01:59:13.290 --> 01:59:16.290
It is the blood of Jesus that saves you.

1351
01:59:16.290 --> 01:59:17.290
And you must stay with him.

1352
01:59:17.290 --> 01:59:20.290
You just have to stay with him.

1353
01:59:20.290 --> 01:59:23.290
For it is not your potential that verse 17 says.

1354
01:59:23.290 --> 01:59:24.290
He belonged with us.

1355
01:59:24.290 --> 01:59:26.290
He was with us together.

1356
01:59:26.290 --> 01:59:29.290
You can seem like a great father.

1357
01:59:29.290 --> 01:59:32.290
You can seem like a great husband.

1358
01:59:32.290 --> 01:59:35.290
You can seem like a great man in God's kingdom.

1359
01:59:35.290 --> 01:59:38.290
Verse 17, he belonged with us.

1360
01:59:38.290 --> 01:59:40.290
In our group.

1361
01:59:40.290 --> 01:59:42.290
He had the same task as us.

1362
01:59:42.290 --> 01:59:45.290
Do you think Jesus made a mistake by the way?

1363
01:59:45.290 --> 01:59:50.290
That Jesus thought to himself, oh why did I allow him in my group?

1364
01:59:51.290 --> 01:59:54.290
Jesus allowed him in his group.

1365
01:59:54.290 --> 01:59:57.290
Because he had a chance to obey.

1366
01:59:59.290 --> 02:00:01.290
Some people, I had a question recently.

1367
